INT. NIGHT FERRY CAR DECK - NIGHT

Cars parked in rows. Engine drone. Fluorescent tubes flicker. Salt wind slaps through the half-open bow.

A MAN in a grey raincoat sits alone in a dented Volvo, engine off. Hands on the wheel. Watching the mirror.

A woman walks the aisle between cars. Torch in hand. Ferry uniform. Her badge reads P. LINDQVIST.

She raps the glass.

The Man lowers the window two inches.

LINDQVIST
Sir. Passengers must leave the deck during crossing.

MAN
I'm fine here.

LINDQVIST
It's a rule.

MAN
I'm unwell. I'd rather not climb the stairs.

She studies him. Torch beam on his hands. On the wet hem of the coat.

LINDQVIST
You're soaked, sir.

MAN
Seasick.

LINDQVIST
We haven't left the pier.

The Man says nothing.

A third figure steps from behind a pickup, thirty feet back. A young deckhand, cap pulled low.

DECKHAND KOFI ASANTE, 20s, sees them. Stops.

KOFI
Pia? Everything okay?

LINDQVIST
Kofi. Stay there.

KOFI
Who's he?

LINDQVIST
I'm finding out.

The Man opens his door slowly. Steps out. Rain on the deck. He holds his palms up.

MAN
I'm not armed.

LINDQVIST
Nobody said you were.

MAN
Nobody had to.

Kofi edges closer, hand on a pry bar at his belt.

KOFI
Pia, his boot. There's blood.

Lindqvist looks down. A dark smear at the heel.

LINDQVIST
Sir. Whose is that?

MAN
Mine.

LINDQVIST
Show me where you're hurt.

MAN
I'm not.

KOFI
Then it's not yours.

A long pause. The Man exhales. Shoulders drop.

MAN
Her name was Annelie.

LINDQVIST
Annelie who?

MAN
My sister.

KOFI
Where is she?

MAN
At the terminal. In the lockers.

Lindqvist's torch wavers. Kofi swears under his breath.

LINDQVIST
(into her radio)
Bridge, this is Lindqvist. Hold the ramp. Call the harbour police.

The radio hisses. Lindqvist presses the key again.

LINDQVIST
Hold the ramp. Now.

The Man sits down on the wet deck beside his car. Folds his hands in his lap.

MAN
I'm Henrik. Henrik Bjornsson. You'll want that for your report.

LINDQVIST
Stay where you are, Mr. Bjornsson.

HENRIK
I'm not going anywhere. I couldn't if I tried.

Kofi lowers the pry bar. Lindqvist keeps the torch on Henrik's face, steady.

LINDQVIST
Kofi. Blanket from the lifeboat store.

KOFI
Pia, he--

LINDQVIST
He's cold, Kofi. Get the blanket.

Kofi runs. His steps ring down the deck.

HENRIK
(quietly)
She'd have liked the crossing.

Lindqvist says nothing. The engines catch, a long low shudder through the steel. The ramp groans, halts, and holds.

HENRIK (CONT'D)
Is it always this loud?

LINDQVIST
You get used to it.

HENRIK
I don't think I will.

Blue lights bloom against the bow doors. Rain slants through them.

Lindqvist crouches, torch lowered. Henrik looks up at her, face wet and open, nothing left in it to hide.

KOFI (O.S.)
(running back)
I've got it! I've got the blanket!

He skids in, drapes it around Henrik's shoulders. Henrik pulls it tight.

HENRIK
Thank you.

KOFI
(stiff)
Yeah.

Footsteps on the ramp. Many. Lindqvist stands.

LINDQVIST
Here we go.

She steps aside. The police come into the light.
